out.update({"updated_at":datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(),"status":"calibrated_spatial_localization_supported; causal_mechanism_unresolved; no_new_solver_run","summary":summary,"calibration_all_pass":all(s["csv_calibration_pass"] for s in out["snapshots"]),"conclusion":"The large native water-phase imbalance in these four snapshots is concentrated in a few interface cells of the last outlet-adjacent column, rather than distributed through the unforced core. This identifies where the residual is produced; it does not yet identify the boundary-face or limiter mechanism.","plain_language":"The short-wave test's conservation discrepancy is almost entirely at the downstream edge of the tank, near the water surface. It is not evidence that the selected foil mesh is inadequate.","limits":["Four selected instantaneous snapshots, not a time-integrated budget or full propagation validation.","Signed percentages can exceed 100% because other locations contribute with the opposite sign; absolute contribution shares are supplied separately.","Alpha near 0 or 1 is not proof of clipping. Cell-centre positive streamwise velocity does not establish the sign of every outlet face flux.","Integrated boundary flux does not reveal simultaneous local inflow and outflow; face-resolved values are required.","Density-weighted phase residual cancellation does not clear the unchanged 0.01% inlet mass-review criterion.","The M09 calm-template decision is unchanged; original foil-wave force comparisons and M10 wave-grid validation remain pending."],"next_recommended_diagnostic":{"name":"Outlet-interface boundary-face audit through the known imbalance event","status":"prepared recommendation only; campaign remains paused and no CFD has been launched","type":"reporting-only controlled replay; no numerical or boundary-condition change","comparison_source":"Preserved original R4 checkpoint_t0.500.sim","baseline":"R14 pressure-tolerance setup, SO1ms10inner, pressure AMG0.01, VOF AMG0.1, all other settings unchanged","bounded_window_s":[0.5,0.63],"purpose":"Distinguish outlet face backflow/prescribed phase interaction from an interior phase update or limiter contribution before choosing another numerical change.","required_observations":["Export unsmoothed outlet face outward mass flux for each phase, normal velocity, face area, face and adjacent-cell water fraction, pressure, and actual backflow/phase boundary option getters.","Capture all inner iterations at0.612,0.617,0.618,0.625s; include the last two x columns and the calibrated native global reports.","Retain and enumerate actual correction/limiter fields supported by the installed solver; document units, no guessed field names and no uncalibrated spatial budget.","Keep boundary net flux and positive/negative face contributions separately; preserve native+BDF2 budgets and gauges."],"decision_rule":"Only if the face-resolved evidence links the spike to a specific boundary setting should the next numerical attempt change that single setting. Do not choose another tighter AMG tolerance, more inner iterations, reduced time step, or combined outlet/forcing change without new evidence.","guards_unchanged":["0.01% inlet mass-review threshold","finite alpha/speed/time/resource guards","source and every attempt preserved","no force/long-propagation admission"]},"primary_local_evidence":["wave_pressure_tolerance_r14_review.json","professor_wave_post_r13_followup_review.json","wave_phase_budget_probe_r10_review.json","wave_outlet_local_documentation.json"],"source_note":"Installed Siemens VOF Waves Guidelines (GUID-886FDC20-F60F-4875-8D46-109D27E6ED08) documents flat-wave pressure/volume-fraction outlet profiles; present localization alone is insufficient to discard this boundary strategy."})
